            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive and antidiarrhoeal activity of Zanthoxylum rhetsa.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>340-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The methanolic extract of the Zanthoxylum rhetsa Roxb. stem bark, given by oral route to mice at doses of 250 and 500 mg/kg, significantly reduced the abdominal contraction induced by acetic acid and the diarrhoeal episodes induced by castor oil in mice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
